Adithya Chandra created KAFKA-16083:
---------------------------------------

             Summary: Exclude throttle time when expiring inflight requests=
 on a connection
                 Key: KAFKA-16083
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-16083
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: clients
            Reporter: Adithya Chandra


When expiring inflight requests, the network client does not take throttle =
time into account. If a connection has multiple inflight requests (default =
of 5) and each request is throttled then some of the requests can incorrect=
ly marked as expired. Subsequently the connection is closed and the client =
establishes a new connection to the broker. This behavior leads to unnecess=
ary connections to the broker, leads to connection storms and increases lat=
encies.=C2=A0



