Hi Mickael,

Thanks for bringing this up.

The main motivation given in KIP-653 for moving to log4j 2.x is that log=
4j 1.x is no longer supported. But since we moved to reload4j, which is =
still supported, that isn't a concern any longer.

To be clear, I'm not saying we shouldn't upgrade, but I'm just trying to=
 explain why I think there hasn't been as much interest in this lately. =
I see this as a "cool feature" rather than as a must-do.

If we still want to do this for 4.0, it would be good to understand whet=
her there's any work that has to land in 3.8. Do we have to get KIP-719 =
into 3.8 so that we have a reasonable deprecation period?

Also, if we do upgrade, I agree with Ismael that we should consider goin=
g to log4j3. Assuming they have a non-beta release by the time 4.0 is re=
ady.

best,
Colin

