The javadocs for=C2=A0{{commitAsync()}}=C2=A0(w/o callback) say:
@throws org.apache.kafka.common.errors.FencedInstanceIdException if this co=
nsumer instance gets fenced by broker.
=C2=A0
If no callback is passed into=C2=A0{{{}commitAsync(){}}}, no offset commit =
callback invocation is submitted. However, we only check for a=C2=A0{{Fence=
dInstanceIdException}}=C2=A0when we execute a callback. It seems to me that=
 with=C2=A0{{commitAsync()}}=C2=A0we would not throw at all when the consum=
er gets fenced.
In any case, we need a unit test that verifies that the=C2=A0{{FencedInstan=
ceIdException}}=C2=A0is thrown for each version of=C2=A0{{{}commitAsync(){}=
}}.
