Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-16190) Member should send full heartbeat
 when rejoining
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Lianet Magrans created KAFKA-16190:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Member should send full heartbeat when rejoining
                 Key: KAFKA-16190
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-16190
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Sub-task
          Components: clients, consumer
            Reporter: Lianet Magrans


The heartbeat request builder should make sure that all fields are sent in the heartbeat request when the consumer rejoins (currently the HeartbeatRequestManager request builder is only reset on failure scenarios). 
This should fix the issue that a client that is subscribed to a topic and gets fenced, should try to rejoin providing the same subscription it had. 



