Hi Kafka Dev Team,
Could you please help us with our problem.

In our POC, if one of the kafka consumer(Service) shuts down or crashes the=
n post restart of service none of the messages are getting consumed by the =
crashed Service.
Other services are consuming without any issues.


[cid:image001.png@01DA53BC.B5237D90]


One of service crash/Shutdown
[cid:image002.png@01DA53BC.B5237D90]

If we rename the Kafka consumer group name and start the service then messa=
ges start consuming.
[cid:image003.png@01DA53BC.B5237D90]


Consumer configuration :

{
                delay:1000
                timeout:0
                topic-name=3D test
                handlers=3D["Listener"]
                source=3D"kafka-consumer"
                enable_auto_commit=3D"false"
                group=3D"Consumer-Group-1"
            }

local-kafka-consumer =3D {
                                            server=3D "{kafka-hostname}:{ka=
fka-port}"
                                                       deserializer=3D"org.=
apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringDeserializer"
                                           auto_offset_reset=3D"latest"
                                           enable_auto_commit=3D"true"
                                           maxRequestSize=3D20971520
                                            }


Thanks,
Santhosh Aditya



--_000_CY8PR07MB95711D35651F5358839FE056E97D2CY8PR07MB9571namp_
