When creating a topic in KRaft cluster, a config value returned in CreateTo=
picsResult is different than what you get from describe topic configs, if t=
he config was set in broker.properties or controller.properties or in both =
but with different values.=C2=A0

=C2=A0

For example, start a broker with `segment.bytes` set to 573741824 in the pr=
operties file and then create a topic, the CreateTopicsResult contains:

ConfigEntry(name=3Dsegment.bytes, value=3D1073741824, source=3DDEFAULT_CONF=
IG, isSensitive=3Dfalse, isReadOnly=3Dfalse, synonyms=3D[], type=3DINT, doc=
umentation=3Dnull)

=C2=A0because the controller was started without setting this config.=C2=A0

However when you describe configurations for the same topic, the config val=
ue set by the broker is returned:

Create topic configsConfigEntry(name=3Dsegment.bytes, value=3D573741824, so=
urce=3DSTATIC_BROKER_CONFIG, isSensitive=3Dfalse, isReadOnly=3Dfalse, synon=
yms=3D[], type=3Dnull, documentation=3Dnull)

=C2=A0

Vice versa, if the controller is started with this config set to a differen=
t value, the create topic request returns the value set by the controller a=
nd then when you describe the config for the same topic, you get the value =
set by the broker. This makes it confusing to understand which value being =
is used.



